  are loaded only to decode an MP3; without the jar an MP3 is refused as any
  format the backend does not read is, with an UnsupportedOperationException
  naming the jar, and WAV and Ogg Vorbis decode as before. Excluding it removes
  one LGPL component, not every one: OpenAL Soft, above, is LGPL too, and the
  backend always ships it.

