Big Buck Bunny: a ten-second excerpt, H.264 picture and AAC sound
  (c) copyright 2008, Blender Foundation
  https://peach.blender.org/ and https://www.bigbuckbunny.org/
  Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 Unported:
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/
  Full text in media/LICENSE-CC-BY-3.0.txt. The excerpt and that text also
  travel inside the limn-demo jar (limn/demo/media/), so the program that plays
  it from its coordinate carries its attribution with it.

  Cut from the Blender Foundation's own 640x360 file, ten seconds of it, with
  nothing encoded again; provenance and the digest are in media/README.md.

  It exists because the FFmpeg build this project ships carries no H.264
  encoder and never will (that encoder is x264, which is GPL), so a clip
  exercising the decoder cannot be produced by this project.

  Note on patents: FFmpeg states that it does not know whether its code uses
  patented algorithms. Distributing a decoder for a standardised codec may
  attract obligations from a patent pool in some jurisdictions, independently of
  the copyright licence above. See docs/adr/011-ffmpeg-licence-and-linking.md §5.
